<rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom" xmlns:media="http://search.yahoo.com/mrss/" xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/"><channel><language>en</language><title>France 24 - International breaking news, top stories and headlines</title><description>Breaking news and world news from France 24 on Business, Sports, Culture. Video news. News from the US, Europe, Asia Pacific, Africa, Middle East, America</description><link>https://www.france24.com/en/</link><lastBuildDate>Tue, 22 Sep 2026 13:27:10 GMT</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://www.france24.com/en/rss" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><category>Entre Nous</category><title>Nutrition expert shares easy steps to healthier eating</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/entre-nous/20260922-nutrition-expert-shares-easy-steps-to-healthier-eating</link><description>
In this edition we're looking at how to eat healthier. We speak to Cynthia Ka, the author of "Mes assiettes naturo". Cynthia says cooking is your pharmacy and doing your weekly shopping is a powerful act. We find out what her go-to recipe is and how we can all make the change to healthier eating. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/713da01a-b67e-11f1-8006-557acd7c815c/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-8132248796ab26ff0552d39-30971946.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/713da01a-b67e-11f1-8006-557acd7c815c/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-8132248796ab26ff0552d39-30971946.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">14cb924a-b67b-11f1-857f-89deaa891193</guid><pubDate>Tue, 22 Sep 2026 13:02:00 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Amanda ALEXANDER</dc:creator></item><item><category>Business</category><title>New report tackles problem of governments' overreliance on consulting firms</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/business/20260922-new-report-tackles-problem-of-governments-overreliance-on-consulting-firms</link><description>
Dependence on consulting firms is a growing trend among governments globally. Left unchecked, it can have a negative impact due to high costs or transparency issues. Such dependence came to the fore in France a few years ago, when the Macron government was criticised for its close ties with US consulting giant McKinsey. UNESCO's Inclusive Policy Lab, headed by Iulia Sevciuc, has established a new blueprint to tackle this problem. She spoke to us in Business.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/fd93d316-b67b-11f1-9978-d382746d948a/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-12986392156ab26bd35af695-68738565.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/fd93d316-b67b-11f1-9978-d382746d948a/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-12986392156ab26bd35af695-68738565.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">8bdd51da-b67a-11f1-ab3e-29550f28a9ba</guid><pubDate>Tue, 22 Sep 2026 12:35:18 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Charles PELLEGRIN</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>New book by Princess Diana's brother sparks royal ruckus</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260922-new-book-by-princess-diana-s-brother-sparks-royal-ruckus</link><description>
A new book published Tuesday by the brother of the late Princess Diana has made headlines around the world with its damning allegations about Diana's ex-husband, now King Charles III, and reopened decades-old wounds within Britain's royal family. France 24's correspondent in London Benedicte Paviot has the details.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/1fd4ba02-b67d-11f1-9150-d5a6f2570fbe/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260922-131500-132010-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/1fd4ba02-b67d-11f1-9150-d5a6f2570fbe/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260922-131500-132010-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">26f25132-b67d-11f1-9444-3188018ec12f</guid><pubDate>Tue, 22 Sep 2026 12:09:57 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Macron calls on EU to tackle soaring energy prices</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260922-macron-calls-on-eu-to-tackle-soaring-energy-prices</link><description>
Emmanuel Macron has written to the EU Commission president, Ursula von der Leyen, calling on Brussels to take immediate action to lower energy prices. They have been on the rise as the conflict in the Middle East spreads, and as Ukraine's attacks on Russian diesel refineries continue.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/99f9ebe6-b67c-11f1-bb2d-1d61c7110e09/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260922-131311-131500-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/99f9ebe6-b67c-11f1-bb2d-1d61c7110e09/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260922-131311-131500-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">a05a5886-b67c-11f1-93fe-23119fd2b024</guid><pubDate>Tue, 22 Sep 2026 12:08:48 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Media ban 'an escalation even for Trump'</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260922-media-ban-an-escalation-even-for-trump</link><description>
CNN, MS NOW and Politico on Monday sued President Donald Trump’s administration days after they were barred from White House grounds, calling the selective ban — based on the content of their coverage — a “blatant violation” of the First Amendment. The extraordinary ban represents an escalation of Trump’s long-running efforts to restrict news coverage he finds objectionable, says France 24’s Kethevane Gorjestani.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/fa1af85e-b67b-11f1-ba6f-d5a6f2570fbe/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260922-120418-120712-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/fa1af85e-b67b-11f1-ba6f-d5a6f2570fbe/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260922-120418-120712-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">ff4920d0-b67b-11f1-9219-03d1c19ef9ac</guid><pubDate>Tue, 22 Sep 2026 12:07:29 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Focus</category><title>Climate change, overfishing: Lake Chad sees fish stocks dwindle</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/focus/20260922-climate-change-overfishing-lake-chad-sees-fish-stocks-dwindle</link><description>
People living in Chad’s Lake Province are bearing the brunt of climate change. The region and the communities that have developed there have historically depended on this vast body of water. Fishing, first and foremost, but also farming, are the pillars of local livelihoods. Yet both are increasingly disrupted by erratic weather patterns: dwindling fish stocks, damaged farmland and a rising cost of living.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/e539da66-b5e2-11f1-a66a-1d61c7110e09/w:1024/p:16x9/FR-NW-OOV-ECRAN-FREEZE-TCHAD-LAC-BAIN-Lauren.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/e539da66-b5e2-11f1-a66a-1d61c7110e09/w:1024/p:16x9/FR-NW-OOV-ECRAN-FREEZE-TCHAD-LAC-BAIN-Lauren.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">da056024-b5e3-11f1-88dc-17fcf9aa119c</guid><pubDate>Tue, 22 Sep 2026 11:30:56 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Harold GIRARD</dc:creator></item><item><category>Spotlight</category><title>Trump admin's hardline deportation policy an 'attempt to break the global refugee and asylum system'</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20260922-trump-admin-s-hardline-deportation-policy-an-attempt-to-break-the-global-refugee-and-asylum-system</link><description>
François Picard is pleased to welcome Washington Post national security reporter Adam Taylor. The Forbidden Stories consortium, involving France 24 and 25 other media outlets, has spent six months investigating the thousands of people abruptly deported from the United States to third countries, amid concerns over due process and their ability to challenge their removal. The investigation examines how the Trump administration has made deportation a major focus of both US immigration and foreign policy.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f7930ebc-b673-11f1-bcba-4d220c210a04/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260921-180124-181318-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f7930ebc-b673-11f1-bcba-4d220c210a04/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260921-180124-181318-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">c463b046-b678-11f1-bd73-378746670215</guid><pubDate>Tue, 22 Sep 2026 11:28:40 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>François PICARD</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Wars, AI and climate on agenda as world leaders meet at UN</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260922-wars-ai-and-climate-on-agenda-as-world-leaders-meet-at-un</link><description>
In the face of an unrelenting succession of global crises, this year's United Nations General Assembly has chosen as its theme “Restoring trust, managing transformation: A United Nations that delivers for all”. From AI to climate change and ongoing wars, France 24 takes a look at what’s on the agenda.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/833b98b8-b673-11f1-8919-557acd7c815c/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260922-103157-103345-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/833b98b8-b673-11f1-8919-557acd7c815c/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260922-103157-103345-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">89296b74-b673-11f1-98d8-5183fd744011</guid><pubDate>Tue, 22 Sep 2026 11:17:32 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Americas feel effects of record El Nino</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260922-americas-feel-effects-of-record-el-nino</link><description>
The El Nino–Southern Oscillation this year equaled its record intensity, according to specialists, and could yet reach record levels. The weather phenomenon's influence has already been felt across the world, with drought, wildfires, food shortages and sharp rises in water temperatures. The state of California has declared a state of emergency due to El Nino and the effects have been felt all over the Americas.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/3a08f8a4-b676-11f1-b7cb-1d61c7110e09/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260922-104005-104130-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/3a08f8a4-b676-11f1-b7cb-1d61c7110e09/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260922-104005-104130-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">3f3777ec-b676-11f1-a7d2-798ef0812789</guid><pubDate>Tue, 22 Sep 2026 11:16:03 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Perspective</category><title>Greenland agreement 'doesn't really give the US many more rights', expert says</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/perspective/20260922-greenland-agreement-doesn-t-really-give-the-us-many-more-rights-expert-says</link><description>
As the US, Denmark and Greenland itself sign an agreement on Greenland's security, we've been asking what difference it will actually make. Our expert says the deal won't really give the US many more rights, but that US President Donald Trump wanted to prevent at all costs the tiny risk of Greenland turning towards China. He adds that for Trump voters, if you inflate the risk, people will talk about it and see you're acting. We spoke in Perspective to Mikaa Blugeon-Mered, Senior Researcher on Hydrogen and Arctic Affairs at the Canada Research Chair in Clean Hydrogen at the University of Québec Trois Rivières.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/816fea02-b673-11f1-8b80-d5a6f2570fbe/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-8640513086ab25d97164463-88773820.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/816fea02-b673-11f1-8b80-d5a6f2570fbe/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-8640513086ab25d97164463-88773820.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">463b7f08-b666-11f1-b21b-7dfa233bdef3</guid><pubDate>Tue, 22 Sep 2026 11:07:30 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Stuart NORVAL</dc:creator></item><item><category>Americas</category><title>Top TV networks – including Fox – revolt in solidarity with media banned by Trump</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260922-top-tv-networks-%E2%80%93-including-fox-%E2%80%93-revolt-in-solidarity-with-media-banned-by-trump</link><description>
The top five US television networks staged a revolt on Monday when they effectively boycotted coverage of President Donald Trump to protest his decision to ban three news outlets from the White House. "No administration should restrict a news organization because it objects to its reporting," ABC, CBS, CNN, Fox and NBC said in a joint statement.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/af7d2fce-b66c-11f1-af8c-557acd7c815c/w:1024/p:16x9/CNN.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/af7d2fce-b66c-11f1-af8c-557acd7c815c/w:1024/p:16x9/CNN.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">eebec04e-b66c-11f1-9ce1-8f7c3b86517d</guid><pubDate>Tue, 22 Sep 2026 10:59:33 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/af7d2fce-b66c-11f1-af8c-557acd7c815c/w:1024/p:16x9/CNN.jpg">© Jose Luis Magana, AP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Donald Trump: US outlets boycott Trump over media ban</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260922-donald-trump-us-outlets-boycott-trump-over-media-ban</link><description>
During a ribbon-cutting ceremony for a new helipad at the White House on Monday, Donald Trump made a brief statement that was inaudible.
 
In response to Trump’s decision to bar MS NOW, CNN and Politico from the White House, US television networks, including ABC, CBS, NBC and Fox News, suspended their pooled coverage of the president.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/8bca0478-b674-11f1-9b71-1d61c7110e09/w:1024/p:16x9/TRUMP-BOYCOTT-MEDIA-thumbnail.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/8bca0478-b674-11f1-9b71-1d61c7110e09/w:1024/p:16x9/TRUMP-BOYCOTT-MEDIA-thumbnail.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">d125a000-b673-11f1-8a10-5183fd744011</guid><pubDate>Tue, 22 Sep 2026 10:53:16 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Hope and scepticism among youth as Morocco goes to the polls</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260922-hope-and-scepticism-among-youth-as-morocco-goes-to-the-polls</link><description>
With just a day to go before legislative elections on September 23, young Moroccans are torn between hope and scepticism ahead of the crucial vote. Nearly 16 million Moroccans are set to elect their representatives to the National Assembly in the country’s first legislative elections since the Gen Z protests which swept through Morocco almost a year ago.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/8543387a-b671-11f1-9950-e554abee39f5/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260922-102327-102513-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/8543387a-b671-11f1-9950-e554abee39f5/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260922-102327-102513-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">8a3293b2-b671-11f1-9a46-0bff92c9c06f</guid><pubDate>Tue, 22 Sep 2026 10:46:02 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>UK to offer Saudi Arabia aerial refueling to counter Houthi attacks</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260922-uk-to-offer-saudi-arabia-aerial-refueling-to-counter-houthi-attacks</link><description>
A British tanker plane will provide "defensive" air-to-air refuelling for Saudi warplanes to help the country defend against Houthi strikes, the UK government confirmed late Monday. The show of solidarity follows a Saudi request for military support after the Houthis increased drone and missile attacks on it in recent weeks alongside a lightning offensive to capture Yemen's Red Sea coast.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/c01e241a-b670-11f1-82e6-d382746d948a/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260922-102117-102308-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/c01e241a-b670-11f1-82e6-d382746d948a/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260922-102117-102308-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">c549bcce-b670-11f1-b7f4-7d8a76e75fce</guid><pubDate>Tue, 22 Sep 2026 10:44:22 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>EU fails to reach deal to lift sanctions on Russian oligarchs</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260922-eu-fails-to-reach-deal-to-lift-sanctions-on-russian-oligarchs</link><description>
EU countries failed Monday to finalise a deal that involved lifting sanctions on Russian oligarchs Alisher Usmanov and Mikhail Fridman, Multiple diplomats said earlier that member states had reached a provisional agreement to take the pair off the EU's blacklist as part of a compromise to extend sanctions on almost 3,000 other individuals and entities over the Ukraine war. France 24's Dave Keating has more from Brussels.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/d3ea1b90-b66e-11f1-86b7-1d61c7110e09/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260922-101750-102046-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/d3ea1b90-b66e-11f1-86b7-1d61c7110e09/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260922-101750-102046-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">dcaa7d92-b66e-11f1-ad90-0b839ddc6763</guid><pubDate>Tue, 22 Sep 2026 10:38:21 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Flights cancelled, evacuations urged as Typhoon Dujuan hits Japan</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260922-flights-cancelled-evacuations-urged-as-typhoon-dujuan-hits-japan</link><description>
More than one million people were under evacuation advisories in Japan early Tuesday and hundreds of flights have been cancelled as Typhoon Dujuan brushed past Tokyo, bringing torrential rains, flooding and landslides to the region.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/bc93f50c-b66d-11f1-95d9-d382746d948a/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260922-101614-101726-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/bc93f50c-b66d-11f1-95d9-d382746d948a/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260922-101614-101726-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">c2256596-b66d-11f1-a6b5-6ffb49795cf8</guid><pubDate>Tue, 22 Sep 2026 10:29:04 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Macron, Trump hold 'constructive' talks ahead of UN General Assembly</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260922-macron-trump-hold-constructive-talks-ahead-of-un-general-assembly</link><description>
French President Emmanuel Macron said on Monday he had "very constructive" talks with his US counterpart Donald Trump on the conflicts in the Middle East and Ukraine as they met in New York ahead of the annual gathering of world leaders at the United Nations General Assembly. France 24’s Philip Turle takes a closer look at what came out of Macron and Trump’s bilateral meeting and what to look out for at the UN later today.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/49ec78cc-b66c-11f1-bd60-d382746d948a/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260922-100127-100921-CS-01.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/49ec78cc-b66c-11f1-bd60-d382746d948a/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260922-100127-100921-CS-01.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">4f294a9a-b66c-11f1-980f-a79ef474e67c</guid><pubDate>Tue, 22 Sep 2026 10:23:54 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Americas</category><title>Live: Guterres calls for UN Security Council reform</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260922-live-guterres-to-open-un-general-assembly-in-final-speech-of-his-mandate</link><description>
UN Secretary-General Antonio Guterres opened the General Assembly in New York on Tuesday for the last time before his term ends on December 31. Guterres will be followed at the podium by Brazilian President Luiz Inacio Lula da Silva, US President Donald Trump and French President Emmanuel Macron. Watch his address live on FRANCE 24.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/0a67da0a-b65f-11f1-8029-1d61c7110e09/w:1024/p:16x9/000-A2KA4QZ.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/0a67da0a-b65f-11f1-8029-1d61c7110e09/w:1024/p:16x9/000-A2KA4QZ.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">1133f350-b664-11f1-9bff-694aa5a37c35</guid><pubDate>Tue, 22 Sep 2026 10:09:35 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/0a67da0a-b65f-11f1-8029-1d61c7110e09/w:1024/p:16x9/000-A2KA4QZ.jpg">© Timothy A.Clary, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>States settle lawsuit with Paramount, paving way for Warner merger</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260922-states-settle-lawsuit-with-paramount-paving-way-for-warner-merger</link><description>
Twelve states and Hollywood writers challenging Paramount’s buyout of Warner Bros. Discovery agreed to settle their lawsuits on Monday, effectively paving the way for the $81 billion mega merger to cross the finish line, with some new commitments from the company.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/47155c8a-b668-11f1-8bb6-d5a6f2570fbe/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260922-101413-101549-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/47155c8a-b668-11f1-8bb6-d5a6f2570fbe/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260922-101413-101549-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">4c0d69b2-b668-11f1-ad12-212780ed4b27</guid><pubDate>Tue, 22 Sep 2026 10:00:00 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Press Review</category><title>How to break the negative habit of 'toxic multitasking'?</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/press-review/20260922-how-to-break-the-negative-habit-of-toxic-multitasking</link><description>
PRESS REVIEW – Tuesday, September 22: The Moscow Times talks about mobilisation rumours scaring anti-war activists in Russia. Next: The New York Times interviews South Korea's President Lee Jae Myung. Also: why is multitasking bad for the brain and the nervous system? Finally: this year's Fat Bear contest is starting in Alaska. Who's going to be the chonkiest chonk? 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/58106292-b649-11f1-a896-e554abee39f5/w:1024/p:16x9/Anglais-2026-09-22T05-24-48-413Z.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/58106292-b649-11f1-a896-e554abee39f5/w:1024/p:16x9/Anglais-2026-09-22T05-24-48-413Z.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">8e5405ca-b64e-11f1-acd4-415c1b1bf7c5</guid><pubDate>Tue, 22 Sep 2026 09:54:02 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Elitsa GADEVA</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>'Great deal of scepticism' as Trump launches own TV channel</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260922-great-deal-of-scepticism-as-trump-launches-own-tv-channel</link><description>
The White House launched a "Trump TV" stream on Monday evening, days after Trump banned three media outlets from the White House. The White House said the stream will run videos and highlights of what it calls the Trump administration's achievements but critics have compared it to state propaganda networks seen in autocratic countries such as North Korea, reports the Guardian’s Washington bureau chief David Smith.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/e005e66e-b666-11f1-bf4d-e554abee39f5/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260922-101155-101333-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/e005e66e-b666-11f1-bf4d-e554abee39f5/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260922-101155-101333-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">e51f18b4-b666-11f1-b163-756458887374</guid><pubDate>Tue, 22 Sep 2026 09:34:47 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>US networks halt Trump coverage after three media outlets banned</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260922-us-networks-halt-trump-coverage-after-three-media-outlets-banned</link><description>
US television networks on Monday effectively boycotted coverage of President Donald Trump in protest at his decision to ban three leading outlets - CNN, MS NOW and Politico - from the White House. As a result, Trump's opening of his cherished new White House helipad and his trip to the United Nations General Assembly proceeded without live television coverage.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/eb628554-b665-11f1-93ab-d382746d948a/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260922-101013-101153-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/eb628554-b665-11f1-93ab-d382746d948a/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260922-101013-101153-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">f09b7bca-b665-11f1-8a48-8718bd0ecec5</guid><pubDate>Tue, 22 Sep 2026 09:31:36 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>The Debate</category><title>First New York, now Berlin: Why the left turn for major metropolises?</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-debate/20260922-first-new-york-now-berlin-why-the-left-turn-for-major-metropolises</link><description>
There's the inroads of the far right, but also the broader desire for change. Introducing Berlin's answer to Zohran Mamdani: Elif Eralp, who led the far-left Die Linke party's historic win in Sunday's municipal elections in Berlin. We ask if the 45-year-old daughter of Turkish political exiles can push through her promises of rent freezes and nationalisation of private real estate companies. Just like in New York last year, affordable housing was a hot-button issue. It didn't hurt that her party ran a social media-savvy campaign.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/5f7feb3a-b5e8-11f1-9cad-1d61c7110e09/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-20T165634Z-360619873-RC24NNADN54W-RTRMADP-3-GERMANY-ELECTION-BERLIN-LINKE-REACTION.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/5f7feb3a-b5e8-11f1-9cad-1d61c7110e09/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-20T165634Z-360619873-RC24NNADN54W-RTRMADP-3-GERMANY-ELECTION-BERLIN-LINKE-REACTION.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">b7df62c8-b5e4-11f1-b1d9-f14263dd641d</guid><pubDate>Tue, 22 Sep 2026 07:56:32 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>François PICARD</dc:creator></item><item><category>Sports</category><title>Football: France enter new era with Zinédine Zidane</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/sports/20260922-football-france-enter-new-era-with-zin%C3%A9dine-zidane</link><description>
